# 高频词汇 List06
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023恋练有词
# 描述: 高频词汇List06核心词汇

{{schedule}}{/ˈʃedjuːl/}{时间表；安排}{The meeting is scheduled for next Monday.}}
{{scheme}}{/skiːm/}{计划；方案}{The government launched a new housing scheme.}}
{{secure}}{/sɪˈkjʊər/}{安全的；获得}{She secured a position at a top law firm.}}
{{select}}{/sɪˈlekt/}{选择；挑选}{The committee will select the best candidate.}}
{{shift}}{/ʃɪft/}{转变；轮班}{There has been a major shift in public opinion.}}
{{significant}}{/sɪɡˈnɪfɪkənt/}{重要的；显著的}{This is a significant achievement for the team.}}
{{similar}}{/ˈsɪmɪlər/}{相似的；类似的}{The two proposals are remarkably similar.}}
{{simulate}}{/ˈsɪmjuleɪt/}{模拟；假装}{The software can simulate real-world conditions.}}
{{site}}{/saɪt/}{地点；网站}{The construction site is located downtown.}}
{{solution}}{/səˈluːʃn/}{解决方案；溶液}{We need to find a solution to this problem.}}
{{somewhat}}{/ˈsʌmwɒt/}{有点；稍微}{The results were somewhat surprising.}}
{{source}}{/sɔːs/}{来源；源头}{Renewable energy sources include solar and wind.}}
{{specific}}{/spəˈsɪfɪk/}{具体的；特定的}{Can you give me more specific details?}}
{{stable}}{/ˈsteɪbl/}{稳定的；马厩}{The economy has remained relatively stable.}}
{{status}}{/ˈsteɪtəs/}{地位；状态}{What is the current status of the project?}}
{{stimulate}}{/ˈstɪmjuleɪt/}{刺激；激发}{The government hopes to stimulate economic growth.}}
{{strategy}}{/ˈstrætədʒi/}{策略；战略}{The company developed a new marketing strategy.}}
{{stress}}{/stres/}{压力；强调}{Stress can have a negative impact on health.}}
{{structure}}{/ˈstrʌktʃər/}{结构；构造}{The structure of the essay needs improvement.}}
{{submit}}{/səbˈmɪt/}{提交；服从}{Please submit your application before the deadline.}}
{{subsequent}}{/ˈsʌbsɪkwənt/}{随后的；后来的}{Subsequent events proved his prediction correct.}}
{{substantial}}{/səbˈstænʃl/}{大量的；实质的}{The project requires substantial investment.}}
{{substitute}}{/ˈsʌbstɪtjuːt/}{替代品；替代}{Nothing can substitute for hard work.}}
{{sufficient}}{/səˈfɪʃnt/}{足够的；充分的}{Is there sufficient evidence to support this claim?}}
{{summarize}}{/ˈsʌməraɪz/}{总结；概括}{Please summarize the main points of the article.}}
{{supplement}}{/ˈsʌplɪment/}{补充；增补}{Vitamin supplements can help fill nutritional gaps.}}
{{survey}}{/ˈsɜːveɪ/}{调查；测量}{The survey revealed interesting consumer preferences.}}
{{survive}}{/səˈvaɪv/}{幸存；存活}{The company managed to survive the economic downturn.}}
{{suspect}}{/səˈspekt/}{怀疑；嫌疑犯}{Police suspect that the fire was started deliberately.}}
{{sustain}}{/səˈsteɪn/}{维持；支撑}{It is hard to sustain economic growth without innovation.}}
